  ('07e125cf-f482-73e8-a19a-89205f56f2a2', 'b0l', 'question', '{"prompt":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What is a base case and what happens without one?"}]}]},"answer":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The input the function answers directly without calling itself ("},{"type":"text","text":"n == 0","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" for factorial, an empty subtree for a traversal). Without a reachable base case every call pushes another frame and the program dies with a stack overflow ("},{"type":"text","text":"RecursionError","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" in Python after about 1000 frames). Always check the base case against the smallest valid inputs — "},{"type":"text","text":"0","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"text","text":"1","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":", empty."}]}]}}'),
  ('7b1e9369-4f06-72c7-8fa1-a33cad6a0ec1', 'b0m', 'question', '{"prompt":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What is tail recursion and why does it matter?"}]}]},"answer":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A recursive call in tail position: nothing is done after it returns. The frame can be discarded before the call, so an optimising compiler turns it into a jump ("},{"type":"text","text":"O(1)","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" stack), and a programmer can turn it into a loop with two edits: "},{"type":"text","text":"if → while","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":", call → parameter update. Factorial becomes tail recursive by passing the running product as an accumulator. Python, Java and most JavaScript engines do "},{"type":"text","text":"not","marks":[{"type":"italic"}]},{"type":"text","text":" optimise tail calls, so convert by hand when depth matters."}]}]}}'),
  ('0321a89f-7c18-7bd3-bb48-5cd9e87eb677', 'b0n', 'question', '{"prompt":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"How do you find the time complexity of a recursive function?"}]}]},"answer":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Write the recurrence: calls per level × size reduction + work per call. "},{"type":"text","text":"T(n) = T(n−1) + 1 → O(n)","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (factorial), "},{"type":"text","text":"T(n) = T(n/2) + 1 → O(log n)","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (halving, binary search), "},{"type":"text","text":"T(n) = 2T(n−1) + 1 → O(2ⁿ)","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (the double-recursion puzzle, Tower of Hanoi), "},{"type":"text","text":"T(n) = 2T(n/2) + n → O(n log n)","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (merge sort). The Analysis of Algorithms topic covers solving them."}]}]}}'),
  ('494ea455-7b3d-7d84-91fb-98a194beaf70', 'b0o', 'question', '{"prompt":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What is the space complexity of a recursive function?"}]}]},"answer":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"At least the maximum depth of the call stack, because every pending call keeps a frame: "},{"type":"text","text":"O(n)","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" for factorial and "},{"type":"text","text":"print 1..n","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"text","text":"O(log n)","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" for halving functions, "},{"type":"text","text":"O(height)","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" for a tree traversal. Depth, not total number of calls: naive "},{"type":"text","text":"fib(n)","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" makes "},{"type":"text","text":"O(2ⁿ)","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" calls but is only "},{"type":"text","text":"n","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" deep, so it uses "},{"type":"text","text":"O(n)","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" stack."}]}]}}'),
