uns; Python, Java objects, V8"}]]]},"revision":1},{"id":"02ffaabf-4468-7524-a871-51cf88cab35d","type":"callout","position":"a5","content":{"variant":"note","title":"Key point","doc":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Any sort that only "},{"type":"text","text":"compares","marks":[{"type":"italic"}]},{"type":"text","text":" elements needs "},{"type":"text","text":"Ω(n log n)","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" comparisons in the worst case — there are "},{"type":"text","text":"n!","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" orderings and each comparison rules out at most half. Merge, heap and quick sort are optimal in that sense; counting and radix sort beat it only by not comparing (they index on the values)."}]}]}},"revision":1},{"id":"1c4c9e40-be64-7626-859a-df111ffe55f5","type":"heading","position":"a6","content":{"level":1,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Built-in sorting in each language"}]},"revision":1},{"id":"7de10b96-d2f2-78aa-8aca-6f478e5ab5bc","type":"text","position":"a7","content":{"doc":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"In real code you call the library sort. Know what it runs, whether it is stable, and how to pass a key or comparator."}]}]}},"revision":1},{"id":"aed81d30-45df-7545-8945-354f0050c380","type":"table","position":"a8","content":{"hasHeaderRow":true,"rows":[[[{"type":"text","text":"Language"}],[{"type":"text","text":"Call"}],[{"type":"text","text":"Algorithm"}],[{"type":"text","text":"Stable"}],[{"type":"text","text":"Custom order"}]],[[{"type":"text","text":"Python"}],[{"type":"text","text":"sorted(iterable, key=, reverse=)","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" → new list · "},{"type":"text","text":"list.sort()","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" in place"}],[{"type":"text","text":"Timsort"}],[{"type":"text","text":"yes"}],[{"type":"text","text":"key=","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text